IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sta-strata`

-- Strata Titles Act 1985 (WA), with the Strata Titles (General) Regulations 2019 -- the Q&A layer: the questions people
-- ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The baseline (sta-strata.l4) is written from one seat, "the owner of a lot ... and, before settlement, the
-- buyer who is about to become one". The Act treats those two as different people with different questions, so they
-- are two roles here, and two more people the Act puts duties on are added:
--   - the owner of a lot: a member of the strata company (s 14(8)), who pays the levies, votes and is bound by the
--     by-laws (ss 100, 120-126, 44-47, 83, 110, 197, 210);
--   - the buyer of a lot, before and just after settlement: the Part 10 protections (ss 156-164), the certificate
--     (s 110) and the previous owner's arrears (s 100(6));
--   - the seller of a lot: the person s 156 and s 157 put the disclosure duties on, and who bears the buyer's
--     postponement and avoidance (ss 158-164);
--   - the tenant or other occupier of a lot: bound by the by-laws (s 45(1)(c), (3)), under the s 83 duty, and open to
--     enforcement under s 47.
-- The strata company, its council, the scheme developer as such, the Tribunal and its President are never seats: what
-- they may or must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not
-- hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, with one name, type and @desc,
-- across roles too, so the form asks it once. All are BOOLEAN, and FALSE gives `does not arise for you`:
--   - `the strata company says I have broken a by-law`: the breach notice, Tribunal enforcement, the most it can order
--     and a daily penalty (s 47), for the owner and the occupier;
--   - `I paid a contribution late`: the owner's interest (s 100(4)(b));
--   - `the Tribunal has made an order in my strata dispute`: the owner's internal review (s 210);
--   - `the contract of sale has been signed`: what follows signing (ss 3(1), 157-163), for the buyer and the seller;
--   - `the buyer has avoided the contract`: what must be repaid (s 164(2)), for the buyer and the seller.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role takes none: the levy, reserve fund, budget, vote, by-law,
-- s 83, certificate and dispute questions; the buyer's s 156(4) and arrears questions; the seller's s 156 questions.
--
-- The rules are in sta-strata.l4. This module calls them and restates none; where a new role's question needs a rule
-- the baseline does not state from that seat, a helper here builds it from the Act's text and the baseline's functions.
-- For the owner and the buyer, each answer is the baseline export's own, wrapped in a type that can also say `does not
-- arise for you`. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input; the baseline's s 110 duty, a DEONTIC, is not
-- exported here either, and its 14 days are asked as a number.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Strata Titles Act 1985 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme`
    `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one`
    `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme`
    `I rent or occupy a lot in a strata titles scheme, and do not own it`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `within days` HAS `the number of days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Working days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `working days` HAS `the number of working days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Vote answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the vote is cast by` HAS `who casts it` IS A `Who casts my lot's vote`

DECLARE `Variation answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `it is` HAS `the kind of variation` IS A `Notifiable variation`

-- s 157(3): "(a) if the seller becomes aware of the notifiable variation less than 15 working days before the settlement
-- date for the contract -- as soon as practicable; and (b) in any other case -- not later than 10 working days after the
-- seller becomes aware of the notifiable variation."
DECLARE `Notice deadline` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `no notice under s 157(1) is needed`
    `as soon as practicable`
    `not later than 10 working days after you became aware of it`

§§ `Helpers for the seller's questions`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- s 157(1): "If a notifiable variation occurs after a buyer signs a contract ..., the seller must, by notice in writing,
-- inform the buyer". (4): "Subsection (1) does not apply if -- (a) the seller has in the contract informed the buyer of any
-- proposed action or matter that would be a notifiable variation; and (b) the action or matter when completed does not
-- differ from that described in the contract; and (c) the seller gives the buyer written notice of completion ... within
-- the time required by subsection (5)". The kind of variation is the baseline's own (s 3(1)), listed in full with no
-- OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `the variation` IS A `Notifiable variation`
      `the contract foretold it and it matched` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave notice of its completion in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 157(1), (4) -- the seller must give notice of the variation` IF
    CONSIDER `the variation`
    WHEN `a type 1 notifiable variation` THEN NOT (`the contract foretold it and it matched` AND `I gave notice of its completion in time`)
    WHEN `a type 2 notifiable variation` THEN NOT (`the contract foretold it and it matched` AND `I gave notice of its completion in time`)
    WHEN `no notifiable variation` THEN FALSE

-- Division by zero (after the independent check, 6 Nov 2026). The baseline divides by a sum of unit entitlements, which
-- s 37(1) makes the sum of the whole numbers allocated to the lots: a real scheme's sum is never 0, but the form's
-- engine tries 0 for every open number, and a failed evaluation stops it settling a question. These two guards give
-- the baseline's own answer whenever every sum is above 0, and only decide the impossible zero case themselves.
-- s 100(1)(c): contributions "in proportion to the unit entitlements of their respective lots". When the sum is 0 every
-- lot's whole-number entitlement is 0 (none can exceed the sum), so the lot's share by unit entitlement is 0. A share
-- under a by-law basis divides by nothing and is the baseline's answer as it stands.
GIVEN `the fund` IS A `Fund`
      `the amount raised` IS A NUMBER
      `my unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum of entitlements` IS A NUMBER
      `a different basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my by-law share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my contribution, with no unit entitlements guarded` MEANS
    IF `the sum of entitlements` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `How much is my contribution` `the fund` `the amount raised` `my unit entitlement` `the sum of entitlements` `a different basis` `my by-law share`
    ELSE `my contribution when there are no unit entitlements` `the fund` `the amount raised` `a different basis` `my by-law share`

GIVEN `the fund` IS A `Fund`
      `the amount raised` IS A NUMBER
      `a different basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my by-law share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my contribution when there are no unit entitlements` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fund`
    WHEN `the administrative fund` THEN
        IF `a different basis` THEN `the amount raised` TIMES `my by-law share` ELSE 0
    WHEN `the reserve fund` THEN 0

-- s 3(1) "notifiable variation": the type 1 limb on the lot's proportion of the sum of unit entitlements cannot be
-- measured when a sum is 0. Then the baseline is asked with that limb neutral (every entitlement and sum 1, the other
-- facts as given), and its type 2 limb on a changed schedule is applied to the facts as given -- the baseline's own
-- order: type 1 before type 2 before none.
GIVEN `the change` IS A `What changed before settlement`
GIVETH A `Notifiable variation`
`the kind of notifiable variation, with no unit entitlements guarded` MEANS
    IF      `the change`'s `the notified sum of unit entitlements` GREATER THAN 0
        AND `the change`'s `the sum of unit entitlements now` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `What kind of notifiable variation is it` `the change`
    ELSE `the kind when a sum of unit entitlements is 0` `the change` (`What kind of notifiable variation is it` (`the change with the proportion limb neutral` `the change`))

GIVEN `the change` IS A `What changed before settlement`
GIVETH A `What changed before settlement`
`the change with the proportion limb neutral` MEANS `What changed before settlement` WITH
    `the notified area of the lot` IS `the change`'s `the notified area of the lot`
    `the area of the lot now` IS `the change`'s `the area of the lot now`
    `the notified unit entitlement` IS 1
    `the notified sum of unit entitlements` IS 1
    `the unit entitlement now` IS 1
    `the sum of unit entitlements now` IS 1
    `termination proposal papers were served on the seller` IS `the change`'s `termination proposal papers were served on the seller`
    `the scheme plan was modified affecting the lot or common property` IS `the change`'s `the scheme plan was modified affecting the lot or common property`
    `the by-laws were modified` IS `the change`'s `the by-laws were modified`
    `a services contract was entered or varied` IS `the change`'s `a services contract was entered or varied`
    `a lease or licence over common property was granted or varied` IS `the change`'s `a lease or licence over common property was granted or varied`

GIVEN `the change` IS A `What changed before settlement`
      `the kind without the proportion limb` IS A `Notifiable variation`
GIVETH A `Notifiable variation`
`the kind when a sum of unit entitlements is 0` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind without the proportion limb`
    WHEN `a type 1 notifiable variation` THEN `a type 1 notifiable variation`
    WHEN `a type 2 notifiable variation` THEN `a type 2 notifiable variation`
    WHEN `no notifiable variation` THEN
        IF     (NOT (`the change`'s `the unit entitlement now` EQUALS `the change`'s `the notified unit entitlement`))
            OR (NOT (`the change`'s `the sum of unit entitlements now` EQUALS `the change`'s `the notified sum of unit entitlements`))
        THEN `a type 2 notifiable variation`
        ELSE `no notifiable variation`

§§ `For the owner of a lot`

§§§ `ss 14(8), 37(1), 100, 102 -- my contributions, and the budget`

@export How much must I pay as my lot's share of a levy my strata company has raised for its administrative fund or reserve fund (s 100(1)(c), (2)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the fund` IS A `Fund` @desc Which fund the levy is for: the administrative fund or the reserve fund
      `the amount the strata company resolved to raise` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount, in dollars, the strata company resolved to raise from all the lots
      `my lot's unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit entitlement of your lot, from the schedule of unit entitlements
      `the sum of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all the lots in the scheme
      `the by-laws provide a different basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme by-laws set a basis for contributions other than unit entitlement
      `my share under the by-law basis` IS A NUMBER @desc If the by-laws set a different basis: your lot's share under it, as a fraction (for example 0.05); otherwise 0
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must I pay as my lot's share of a levy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN amount (`my contribution, with no unit entitlements guarded` `the fund` `the amount the strata company resolved to raise` `my lot's unit entitlement` `the sum of the unit entitlements` `the by-laws provide a different basis` `my share under the by-law basis`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my strata company keep a reserve fund and a 10 year plan, so that I will be levied for it (s 100(2), (2A), (7); reg 79)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the number of lots in the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots there are in the strata titles scheme
      `the replacement cost` IS A NUMBER @desc The replacement cost, in dollars, of the scheme building (strata scheme) or of the improvements on the common property (survey-strata scheme)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my strata company keep a reserve fund and a 10 year plan` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Must my strata company keep a reserve fund` `the number of lots in the scheme` `the replacement cost`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much interest can my strata company charge me on a contribution I paid late (s 100(4)(b); reg 78)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I paid a contribution late` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid, or have still not paid, a contribution after it fell due
      `the amount unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the contribution, in dollars, left unpaid after it fell due
      `the days it was overdue` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from the due date until it was paid
      `the company has determined a lesser rate or none` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company has resolved that unpaid contributions bear no interest or a lower rate
      `the rate the company determined` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that yearly rate as a fraction (for example 0.05 for 5%, or 0 for no interest); otherwise 0
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much interest can I be charged on a late contribution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `I paid a contribution late`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much interest do I owe` `the amount unpaid` `the days it was overdue` `the company has determined a lesser rate or none` `the rate the company determined`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must a budget that spends on improving or altering the common property be approved by special resolution, so that my vote counts against it (s 102(5); reg 80)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the improvement spending` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars the budget or variation provides for improving or altering the common property beyond repair (not sustainability infrastructure)
      `the number of lots in the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots there are in the strata titles scheme
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must an improvement budget be approved by special resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Must the improvement budget pass by special resolution` `the improvement spending` `the number of lots in the scheme`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my strata company spend money that the approved budget does not authorise, without a further vote (s 102(6); regs 81, 82)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the unbudgeted spending this financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc Total dollars spent this financial year outside the approved budget, including the proposed item
      `the number of lots in the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots there are in the strata titles scheme
      `a per-lot amount was fixed by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company has fixed its own per-lot amount by special resolution
      `the per-lot amount fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that amount per lot in dollars; otherwise 0
      `it improves or alters the common property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the spending is on improving or altering the common property beyond repair (the s 102(5) kind)
      `notice and two quotations were given to owners and first mortgagees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether notice in the approved form, with at least two quotations, went to every owner and first mortgagee
      `the lots objecting within 14 days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots' owners or first mortgagees objected in writing within 14 days
      `the unit entitlement of the lots objecting` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of the lots whose owners or first mortgagees objected
      `the sum of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all the lots in the scheme
      `a court, tribunal or written-law notice requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, the Tribunal or a notice or order under a written law requires the spending
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my strata company spend outside the approved budget` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Can the strata company spend outside the budget` `the unbudgeted spending this financial year` `the number of lots in the scheme` `a per-lot amount was fixed by special resolution` `the per-lot amount fixed` `it improves or alters the common property` `notice and two quotations were given to owners and first mortgagees` `the lots objecting within 14 days` `the unit entitlement of the lots objecting` `the sum of the unit entitlements` `a court, tribunal or written-law notice requires it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 120, 123, 126 -- my lot's vote`

@export Can I cast my lot's vote on this resolution even though I owe the strata company money (s 120(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution` @desc The kind of resolution being voted on
      `the amount I owe the strata company` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars you owe the strata company that are outstanding and recoverable under the Act (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I cast my lot's vote on this resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Can I cast my lot's vote` `the resolution` `the amount I owe the strata company`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who may cast my lot's vote on a resolution of the strata company (ss 120(2), (6), 126)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution` @desc The kind of resolution being voted on
      `the amount I owe the strata company` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars you owe the strata company that are outstanding and recoverable under the Act (0 if none)
      `my lot is subject to a registered mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a registered mortgage over your lot
      `I own the lot with co-owners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the lot together with someone else (for example as joint tenants)
      `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18 years old
GIVETH A `Vote answer`
`Who may cast my lot's vote on this resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `the vote is cast by` (`Who may cast my lot's vote` `the resolution` `the amount I owe the strata company` `my lot is subject to a registered mortgage` `I own the lot with co-owners` `I am under 18`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Did the resolution pass as a special resolution, the kind needed for a conduct by-law that binds me (s 123(4)-(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the number of lots in the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots there are in the strata titles scheme
      `the sum of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all the lots in the scheme
      `14 days' notice of its terms was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every member got 14 days' notice of the terms before voting opened
      `the lots voting for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots' votes were cast in favour
      `the unit entitlement voting for` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of the lots voting in favour
      `the lots voting against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots' votes were cast against
      `the unit entitlement voting against` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of the lots voting against
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Did the resolution pass as a special resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Did it pass as a special resolution` `the number of lots in the scheme` `the sum of the unit entitlements` `14 days' notice of its terms was given` `the lots voting for` `the unit entitlement voting for` `the lots voting against` `the unit entitlement voting against`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 44-46, 83 -- the by-laws and my use of the lot`

@export Is this by-law of my strata scheme invalid against me (s 46)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the by-law` IS A `What the by-law does` @desc What the by-law does, as a set of yes/no facts (the last one is the Tribunal's judgment)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this by-law of my scheme invalid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Is this by-law invalid` `the by-law`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does this by-law bind me as an owner: was it made by the resolution the Act requires, and is it valid (ss 44(2), 45(2), 46)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of by-law` @desc Whether it is a governance by-law or a conduct by-law
      `it passed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the resolution that made it passed as a special resolution
      `it passed without dissent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the resolution that made it passed as a resolution without dissent (no lot voted against)
      `the by-law` IS A `What the by-law does` @desc What the by-law does, as a set of yes/no facts (the last one is the Tribunal's judgment)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this by-law bind me as an owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Does this by-law bind me` `the kind` `it passed as a special resolution` `it passed without dissent` `the by-law`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I in breach of my duty not to interfere unreasonably with other owners' use and enjoyment (s 83)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the way you use (or let others use) the lot or common property interferes with someone lawfully using another lot or the common property
      `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interference is unreasonable, as the Tribunal would find
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I in breach of the use and enjoyment duty, as an owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Am I breaching the use and enjoyment duty` `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 45(4): "The owner, occupier or lessee of a lot ... must take all steps that are reasonable in the circumstances to
-- ensure that every person who they permit to use or who they invite on to the lot or common property complies with
-- bylaws that apply to the owner, occupier or lessee." Asked of the owner, so yes by the question's own terms.
@export Must I take reasonable steps to make sure my visitors and anyone I let use my lot keep the by-laws (s 45(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I make sure my visitors keep the by-laws` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN yes
    WHEN `I rent or occupy a lot in a strata titles scheme, and do not own it` THEN yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 47 -- when I am said to have broken a by-law`

@export Is the by-law breach notice the strata company gave me a valid notice (s 47(2); reg 57)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the strata company says I have broken a by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company, or another owner or occupier, says you have broken a scheme by-law
      `it names the by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice specifies the particular by-law said to be broken
      `it states the facts relied on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it specifies the facts relied on as evidence
      `it states what I must do or stop doing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it specifies what you must do or refrain from doing
      `it carries the regulations' explanation of s 47` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it includes the explanation of s 47 in the form of Schedule 2 to the regulations
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the by-law breach notice I was given valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the strata company says I have broken a by-law`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is the breach notice valid` `it names the by-law` `it states the facts relied on` `it states what I must do or stop doing` `it carries the regulations' explanation of s 47`)
    -- s 47(1)(a), (2): the notice may be given to "a person alleged to have contravened the scheme bylaws", an occupier
    -- included (s 45(1)(c)); the test is the same.
    WHEN `I rent or occupy a lot in a strata titles scheme, and do not own it` THEN
        IF NOT `the strata company says I have broken a by-law`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is the breach notice valid` `it names the by-law` `it states the facts relied on` `it states what I must do or stop doing` `it carries the regulations' explanation of s 47`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the strata company (or another owner or occupier) take me to the Tribunal to enforce a by-law against me (s 47(1)(b), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the strata company says I have broken a by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company, or another owner or occupier, says you have broken a scheme by-law
      `it seriously harmed someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the breach had serious adverse consequences for someone other than you
      `the times I have broken that by-law` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many separate occasions you have broken that particular by-law
      `I broke a valid breach notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given a written breach notice under s 47(1)(a) and then contravened it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be taken to the Tribunal to enforce a by-law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the strata company says I have broken a by-law`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I be taken to the Tribunal over a by-law` `it seriously harmed someone else` `the times I have broken that by-law` `I broke a valid breach notice`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy a lot in a strata titles scheme, and do not own it` THEN
        IF NOT `the strata company says I have broken a by-law`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I be taken to the Tribunal over a by-law` `it seriously harmed someone else` `the times I have broken that by-law` `I broke a valid breach notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most the Tribunal can order me to pay as a penalty for breaking a by-law (s 47(6)(c); reg 58)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the strata company says I have broken a by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company, or another owner or occupier, says you have broken a scheme by-law
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be ordered to pay for breaking a by-law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the strata company says I have broken a by-law`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount `What is the most I can be made to pay for a by-law breach`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy a lot in a strata titles scheme, and do not own it` THEN
        IF NOT `the strata company says I have broken a by-law`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount `What is the most I can be made to pay for a by-law breach`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Tribunal impose a daily penalty on me for a continuing by-law breach (s 47(6)(d))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the strata company says I have broken a by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company, or another owner or occupier, says you have broken a scheme by-law
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be given a daily penalty for a continuing by-law breach` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the strata company says I have broken a by-law`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `Can I be given a daily penalty for a by-law breach`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy a lot in a strata titles scheme, and do not own it` THEN
        IF NOT `the strata company says I have broken a by-law`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `Can I be given a daily penalty for a by-law breach`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 107, 110 -- the certificate of what is owing`

-- s 107(2): a person with a proper interest includes "(a) a member of the strata company" and "(b) a buyer who has entered
-- into a contract for the sale and purchase of a lot", so the owner and the buyer both ask these two.
@export What is the most my strata company may charge me for a s 110 certificate about my lot or the scheme (s 107(4); reg 86)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the strata company must remit GST for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company is required to remit GST on the fee
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be charged for a s 110 certificate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be charged for a certificate` `the strata company must remit GST for it`)
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be charged for a certificate` `the strata company must remit GST for it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many days must the strata company give me the s 110 certificate after my application is duly made (s 110(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days must I be given the s 110 certificate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `within days` `Within how many days must I get the certificate`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN `within days` `Within how many days must I get the certificate`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 197, 210 -- taking a dispute to the Tribunal`

@export Can I, as a lot owner, apply to the State Administrative Tribunal to resolve this dispute as a scheme dispute (s 197)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the dispute` IS A `My dispute` @desc What the dispute is about
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I take this dispute to the Tribunal as a scheme dispute` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Can I take this dispute to the Tribunal` `the dispute`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I apply for internal review of a Tribunal order made in my strata dispute (s 210; reg 162)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Tribunal has made an order in my strata dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Administrative Tribunal has made an order in a strata dispute you are a party to
      `the order was made by a member who is not legally qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal member who made the order is not a legally qualified member
      `the Tribunal gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal gives leave for the internal review
      `days since the order` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the order was made
      `the President extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the President has extended the 28-day period (and you are within it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I apply for internal review of the Tribunal's order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the Tribunal has made an order in my strata dispute`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I seek internal review` `the order was made by a member who is not legally qualified` `the Tribunal gives leave` `days since the order` `the President extended the time`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the buyer of a lot`

§§§ `ss 100(6), 110(3), 156(3), (4) -- before I sign, and the arrears I take on`

@export Having bought my lot, how much of the previous owner's unpaid contributions and interest can the strata company make me pay (s 100(6), s 110(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the arrears at the certificate date` IS A NUMBER @desc Contributions and interest, in dollars, actually unpaid at the date of the s 110 certificate (or at settlement, if you had no certificate)
      `the arrears arising after the certificate date` IS A NUMBER @desc Contributions and interest, in dollars, that fell unpaid after the certificate date and before you became owner (0 if no certificate)
      `I bought with a s 110 certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or your conveyancer) obtained a certificate under s 110(2) for the lot before buying it
      `the arrears the certificate stated` IS A NUMBER @desc The outstanding amount the certificate stated, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of the previous owner's arrears can I be made to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN amount (`How much of the previous owner's arrears must I pay` `the arrears at the certificate date` `the arrears arising after the certificate date` `I bought with a s 110 certificate` `the arrears the certificate stated`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a buyer from the developer, must I also be given the strata company's estimated budget and the developer's contracts and disclosures before I sign (s 156(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the seller is the scheme developer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller of the lot is the scheme developer
      `the scheme is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata titles scheme has been registered
      `the first annual general meeting has been held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company's first annual general meeting has been held
      `the developer's share of the lots` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction of the lots the developer owns (for example 0.6)
      `the developer's share of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction of the total unit entitlement the developer's lots carry
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I also be given the developer's disclosures` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN `yes if` (`Must the developer give me its extra disclosures` `the seller is the scheme developer` `the scheme is registered` `the first annual general meeting has been held` `the developer's share of the lots` `the developer's share of the unit entitlements`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 3(1), 157-163 -- after I sign`

@export Did what changed between my signing and settlement amount to a type 1 or type 2 notifiable variation (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
      `the change` IS A `What changed before settlement` @desc What changed after the buyer signed the contract and before settlement
GIVETH A `Variation answer`
`Did what changed after I signed amount to a notifiable variation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `it is` (`the kind of notifiable variation, with no unit entitlements guarded` `the change`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a buyer, may I postpone settlement because the seller has not given me the required strata information (s 158)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
      `the seller complied with s 156` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave you everything s 156 requires before you signed
      `the seller complied with s 157` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller notified every notifiable variation as s 157 requires (true if none occurred)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I postpone settlement for missing strata information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I postpone settlement` `the seller complied with s 156` `the seller complied with s 157`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I postpone settlement under s 158, by at most how many working days after the seller finally complies?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
GIVETH A `Working days`
`By how many working days may I postpone settlement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `working days` `How many working days may I postpone settlement after compliance`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a buyer, may I avoid my contract because the seller did not give me the s 156 information before I signed (s 159)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
      `the seller complied with s 156` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave you everything s 156 requires before you signed
      `the missing information shows material prejudice to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information not given would disclose material prejudice to you (you must prove it)
      `settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract has already settled
      `the seller has since given substantially complying notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has since given a notice substantially complying with s 156
      `working days since that notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since that late notice was given (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I avoid my contract for missing s 156 information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I avoid for missing disclosure` `the seller complied with s 156` `the missing information shows material prejudice to me` `settlement has happened` `the seller has since given substantially complying notice` `working days since that notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a buyer, may I avoid my contract because of a notifiable variation between signing and settlement (ss 157, 160-162)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
      `the variation` IS A `Notifiable variation` @desc The kind of notifiable variation that occurred
      `the contract foretold it and it matched` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract described the proposed change and the change as completed matched (s 157(4))
      `the seller notified it in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave you notice of it within the time s 157(3) allows
      `the seller has given notice of it at all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has given you notice of the variation at any time
      `working days since the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since that notice was given (0 if none)
      `it materially prejudices me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are materially prejudiced by the variation (you must prove it)
      `settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract has already settled
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I avoid my contract for a notifiable variation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I avoid for a notifiable variation` `the variation` `the contract foretold it and it matched` `the seller notified it in time` `the seller has given notice of it at all` `working days since the notice` `it materially prejudices me` `settlement has happened`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a buyer off the plan, may I avoid my contract because the deposit is not held on trust or the scheme is not registered in time (s 163)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
      `the scheme is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata titles scheme has been registered
      `the contract has the deposit held on trust by a named practitioner or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract requires the deposit to be held on trust for you by a lawyer, real estate agent or settlement agent it names
      `a period for registration was agreed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the seller agreed in writing on a period for registration
      `the agreed period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that period in months; otherwise 0
      `whole months since the date of the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since the contract was signed (by the last party to sign)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I avoid my off-the-plan contract under s 163` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I avoid my off-the-plan contract` `the scheme is registered` `the contract has the deposit held on trust by a named practitioner or agent` `a period for registration was agreed in writing` `the agreed period in months` `whole months since the date of the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 164 -- if the contract is avoided`

@export If I avoid my contract to buy a lot, how much do I get back (s 164(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the buyer has avoided the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has avoided the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot under Part 10 (ss 159-163)
      `the deposit held for me` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars held on your behalf as a deposit by an agent or practitioner
      `other money I paid the seller` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other dollars you paid the seller under the contract
      `rent due for my occupation` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars due to the seller as rent for any time you occupied the lot (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much do I get back if I avoid my contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one` THEN
        IF NOT `the buyer has avoided the contract`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much do I get back` `the deposit held for me` `other money I paid the seller` `rent due for my occupation`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the seller of a lot`

§§§ `s 156 -- before the buyer signs`

-- s 156(1): "Before a buyer signs a contract for the sale and purchase of a lot in a strata titles scheme, the seller of
-- the lot must give the buyer the following" (the scheme documents, minutes, accounts, the lot's unit entitlement,
-- contributions and debts). (5): by a notice in the approved form, or in the contract as the regulations set out. Asked of
-- the seller, so yes by the question's own terms.
@export Before the buyer signs, must I give them the scheme documents, the strata company's details, minutes and accounts, and the lot's unit entitlement, contributions and debts (s 156(1), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I give the buyer the s 156 information before they sign` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 156(4) puts the extra disclosures on the seller "if the scheme developer is the seller of the lot". The baseline's
-- buyer question is the same rule from the other side.
@export As the seller, must I also give the buyer the strata company's estimated budget and the developer's contracts and disclosures before they sign (s 156(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am the scheme developer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the scheme developer of the strata titles scheme
      `the scheme is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata titles scheme has been registered
      `the first annual general meeting has been held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company's first annual general meeting has been held
      `the developer's share of the lots` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction of the lots the developer owns (for example 0.6)
      `the developer's share of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction of the total unit entitlement the developer's lots carry
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I give the buyer the developer's disclosures` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Must the developer give me its extra disclosures` `I am the scheme developer` `the scheme is registered` `the first annual general meeting has been held` `the developer's share of the lots` `the developer's share of the unit entitlements`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 156(6), s 157(6): "the onus of proving that the required information and statements were given in accordance with
-- this section lies on the seller" (and of the s 157 notices).
@export If there is a dispute, must I prove that I gave the buyer the s 156 information and the s 157 notices as the Act requires (s 156(6), s 157(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I prove I gave the buyer the information and notices` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 3(1), 157-162 -- after the buyer signs`

@export Must I give the buyer written notice of this change between signing and settlement (ss 3(1), 157(1), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
      `the change` IS A `What changed before settlement` @desc What changed after the buyer signed the contract and before settlement
      `the contract foretold it and it matched` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract described the proposed change and the change as completed matched (s 157(4))
      `I gave notice of its completion in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the buyer written notice that the foretold change was completed, within the time s 157(5) allows
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I give the buyer notice of this change` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`s 157(1), (4) -- the seller must give notice of the variation` (`the kind of notifiable variation, with no unit entitlements guarded` `the change`) `the contract foretold it and it matched` `I gave notice of its completion in time`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By when must I give the buyer notice of a notifiable variation (s 157(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
      `the change` IS A `What changed before settlement` @desc What changed after the buyer signed the contract and before settlement
      `the contract foretold it and it matched` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract described the proposed change and the change as completed matched (s 157(4))
      `I gave notice of its completion in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the buyer written notice that the foretold change was completed, within the time s 157(5) allows
      `I became aware of it less than 15 working days before the settlement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became aware of the variation less than 15 working days before the settlement date for the contract
GIVETH A `Notice deadline`
`By when must I give the buyer notice of the variation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE IF NOT `s 157(1), (4) -- the seller must give notice of the variation` (`the kind of notifiable variation, with no unit entitlements guarded` `the change`) `the contract foretold it and it matched` `I gave notice of its completion in time`
             THEN `no notice under s 157(1) is needed`
             ELSE IF `I became aware of it less than 15 working days before the settlement date`
                  THEN `as soon as practicable`
                  ELSE `not later than 10 working days after you became aware of it`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the buyer postpone settlement because I have not given the s 156 information or a s 157 notice (s 158)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
      `I gave everything s 156 requires before the buyer signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the buyer everything s 156 requires before they signed
      `I gave every notice s 157 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you notified every notifiable variation as s 157 requires (true if none occurred)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the buyer postpone settlement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I postpone settlement` `I gave everything s 156 requires before the buyer signed` `I gave every notice s 157 requires`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If the buyer postpones settlement under s 158, by at most how many working days after I finally comply?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
GIVETH A `Working days`
`By how many working days may the buyer postpone settlement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `working days` `How many working days may I postpone settlement after compliance`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the buyer avoid the contract because I did not give the s 156 information before they signed (s 159)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
      `I gave everything s 156 requires before the buyer signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the buyer everything s 156 requires before they signed
      `the missing information shows material prejudice to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information not given would disclose material prejudice to the buyer (the buyer must prove it)
      `settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract has already settled
      `I have since given a substantially complying notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since given the buyer a notice substantially complying with s 156
      `working days since that notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since that late notice was given (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the buyer avoid the contract for missing s 156 information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I avoid for missing disclosure` `I gave everything s 156 requires before the buyer signed` `the missing information shows material prejudice to the buyer` `settlement has happened` `I have since given a substantially complying notice` `working days since that notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the buyer avoid the contract because of a notifiable variation between signing and settlement (ss 157, 160-162)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract of sale has been signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has signed the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot
      `the variation` IS A `Notifiable variation` @desc The kind of notifiable variation that occurred
      `the contract foretold it and it matched` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract described the proposed change and the change as completed matched (s 157(4))
      `I notified it in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the buyer notice of it within the time s 157(3) allows
      `I have given notice of it at all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the buyer notice of the variation at any time
      `working days since the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since that notice was given (0 if none)
      `it materially prejudices the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer is materially prejudiced by the variation (the buyer must prove it)
      `settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract has already settled
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the buyer avoid the contract for a notifiable variation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the contract of sale has been signed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I avoid for a notifiable variation` `the variation` `the contract foretold it and it matched` `I notified it in time` `I have given notice of it at all` `working days since the notice` `it materially prejudices the buyer` `settlement has happened`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 164 -- if the buyer avoids the contract`

-- s 164(2): "(a) the buyer may recover from the seller as a debt all money paid by the buyer under the contract; and (b) a
-- person who is holding a deposit ... must repay the deposit ... minus any amount due to the seller as rent". The seller
-- owes the money paid to the seller; the deposit, less rent, comes back from whoever holds it.
@export If the buyer avoids the contract, how much must I repay them myself, as a debt (s 164(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the buyer has avoided the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has avoided the contract for the sale and purchase of the lot under Part 10 (ss 159-163)
      `money the buyer paid me under the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars the buyer paid you under the contract, not counting a deposit held by an agent or practitioner
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must I repay the buyer myself` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme` THEN
        IF NOT `the buyer has avoided the contract`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much do I get back` 0 `money the buyer paid me under the contract` 0)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the tenant or other occupier of a lot`

§§§ `ss 44-46, 83 -- the by-laws and my use of the lot`

-- s 45(1)(c): scheme by-laws may apply to "an occupier or lessee, for the time being, of a lot"; (2) each person to whom
-- they apply must comply; (3) a lease of a lot "is taken to contain an agreement by the lessee that the lessee will comply
-- with the scheme bylaws". Whether the by-law was validly made, and is valid, is the baseline's own test.
@export Does this by-law of the scheme bind me as a tenant or occupier: was it made by the resolution the Act requires, and is it valid (ss 44(2), 45(1)(c), (2), (3), 46)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of by-law` @desc Whether it is a governance by-law or a conduct by-law
      `it passed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the resolution that made it passed as a special resolution
      `it passed without dissent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the resolution that made it passed as a resolution without dissent (no lot voted against)
      `the by-law` IS A `What the by-law does` @desc What the by-law does, as a set of yes/no facts (the last one is the Tribunal's judgment)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this by-law bind me as a tenant or occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy a lot in a strata titles scheme, and do not own it` THEN `yes if` (`Does this by-law bind me` `the kind` `it passed as a special resolution` `it passed without dissent` `the by-law`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a tenant or occupier, am I in breach of my duty not to interfere unreasonably with others' use and enjoyment (s 83)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the way you use (or let others use) the lot or common property interferes with someone lawfully using another lot or the common property
      `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interference is unreasonable, as the Tribunal would find
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I in breach of the use and enjoyment duty, as an occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    -- s 83: "The owner or occupier of a lot must not use, or permit the use of, the lot ..."; the same test.
    WHEN `I rent or occupy a lot in a strata titles scheme, and do not own it` THEN `yes if` (`Am I breaching the use and enjoyment duty` `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
